1
00:00:00,944 --> 00:00:04,095
This is an AI support agent for a WooCommerce

2
00:00:04,095 --> 00:00:05,495
store. It tracks orders,

3
00:00:05,495 --> 00:00:07,246
checks stock, takes new orders,

4
00:00:07,246 --> 00:00:09,697
and routes calls based on business hours.

5
00:00:09,697 --> 00:00:12,148
Let me show you how it works.

6
00:00:16,268 --> 00:00:19,452
First, order tracking. The customer shares an order number

7
00:00:19,452 --> 00:00:22,637
and their email. The agent checks the store's API,

8
00:00:22,637 --> 00:00:24,406
and replies with the status,

9
00:00:24,406 --> 00:00:26,529
the items, and the tracking number.

10
00:00:26,529 --> 00:00:29,713
On the right, you can see each request behind

11
00:00:29,713 --> 00:00:30,421
the scenes.

12
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:37,597
If the email doesn't match the order,

13
00:00:37,597 --> 00:00:39,409
the agent gives a polite,

14
00:00:39,409 --> 00:00:40,859
general answer. That way,

15
00:00:40,859 --> 00:00:43,396
nobody can look up someone else's order.

16
00:00:46,461 --> 00:00:49,671
Next, inventory. The agent reads live stock levels.

17
00:00:49,671 --> 00:00:51,276
For products with sizes,

18
00:00:51,276 --> 00:00:53,282
it checks each size separately,

19
00:00:53,282 --> 00:00:56,492
which is a very common source of mistakes.

20
00:01:08,030 --> 00:01:10,680
The agent can also take an order.

21
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:12,573
It collects the customer's details,

22
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:14,087
confirms them, checks stock,

23
00:01:14,087 --> 00:01:16,737
and creates a pending order in WooCommerce.

24
00:01:27,199 --> 00:01:30,005
Outside business hours, the call isn't transferred.

25
00:01:30,005 --> 00:01:32,810
Instead, the agent takes a callback request:

26
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:36,417
name, phone number, and the reason for the call.

27
00:01:46,237 --> 00:01:49,516
During business hours, the same request goes straight to

28
00:01:49,516 --> 00:01:52,795
a human. The hours and the timezone are simple

29
00:01:52,795 --> 00:01:53,888
settings, not hard-coded.

30
00:01:56,767 --> 00:01:59,374
This demo runs on a test store.

31
00:01:59,374 --> 00:02:01,608
In production, Voiceflow handles the conversation,

32
00:02:01,608 --> 00:02:03,842
and Make runs this same logic.

33
00:02:03,842 --> 00:02:07,194
I'm Hassam Rauf, and I build AI agents and

34
00:02:07,194 --> 00:02:10,545
automations for businesses. If you'd like one for your

35
00:02:10,545 --> 00:02:11,663
store, let's talk.

